    "body": "Fixes #33482.\n\nPreserve UNC and DOS device prefixes when normalizing Windows paths in fast mode, so `vim.loader` can discover and load modules from UNC runtime paths. Keep validation and dot-component resolution skipped, and preserve existing POSIX fast-mode behavior.\n\nAdd filesystem normalization coverage and a loader discovery regression test that does not require a network share.\n\nValidation: native MSVC Release build, real loopback UNC discovery/loading, 18 normalization tests and all 6 loader tests passed. The broader filesystem run passed 57/59; two existing symlink tests fail on this host due to missing privileges. StyLua, EmmyLua and commit lint passed.\n\nProfiling: 15 independent before/after process pairs measured local fast normalization at 1.722→1.767 µs median (+45 ns). Representative local module discovery/loading showed no consistent regression; timings varied. Linux/macOS and the full suite remain untested locally.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-13T13:49:39Z",
